IMPORT prelude
IMPORT daydate
IMPORT `cp60-nouns`
IMPORT `cp60-cross-references`

-- Row il-60. The control holds, and the recorded facts about the finding are what NOTES.md says they are.
-- The finding itself is NOT asserted sound anywhere in this file: its two failing assertions are in cp60-tests-xrefs-red.l4.
-- Every expected value is written from the texts quoted in cp60-cross-references.l4 (the `ext:` and `src:` lines), not from the output of the module.

§ `Tests of what the citing words name and what the target is labelled`

-- Both citations resolve: the label the citing words name is the label of a paragraph or subsection the official page prints.
#ASSERT `the citation resolves in the official text read` (`reference: s 220ג(ג) to paragraph (4) of s 220ד(א)`)
#ASSERT `the citation resolves in the official text read` (`reference: s 220ג(ג) to subsection (ב) of s 220ג`)
#ASSERT (`reference: s 220ג(ג) to paragraph (4) of s 220ד(א)`)'s `the citing words name` EQUALS "220ד(א)(4)"
#ASSERT (`reference: s 220ג(ג) to paragraph (4) of s 220ד(א)`)'s `the target is labelled` EQUALS "220ד(א)(4)"
#ASSERT (`reference: s 220ג(ג) to subsection (ב) of s 220ג`)'s `the citing words name` EQUALS "220ג(ב)"
#ASSERT (`reference: s 220ג(ג) to subsection (ב) of s 220ג`)'s `the target is labelled` EQUALS "220ג(ב)"

§ `Tests of the last day printed in the target`

-- The paragraph's own words print a day; the control subsection's words print none.
#ASSERT `the target prints a last day` (`reference: s 220ג(ג) to paragraph (4) of s 220ד(א)`)
#ASSERT NOT `the target prints a last day` (`reference: s 220ג(ג) to subsection (ב) of s 220ג`)
#ASSERT (`reference: s 220ג(ג) to paragraph (4) of s 220ד(א)`)'s `the last day printed in the target` EQUALS JUST (Date 31 7 2025)
#ASSERT (`reference: s 220ג(ג) to subsection (ב) of s 220ג`)'s `the last day printed in the target` EQUALS NOTHING
-- The first day certainly after the printed day is the day after it.
#ASSERT (`reference: s 220ג(ג) to paragraph (4) of s 220ד(א)`)'s `the first day certainly after the printed day` EQUALS JUST (Date 1 8 2025)
#ASSERT Day (Date 1 8 2025) EQUALS Day (Date 31 7 2025) + 1

§ `Tests of the days on which the target stands, by its own printed last day`

-- From 1 August 2025, certainly past the printed day on either reading of "until the day": JUST FALSE.
#ASSERT `the target stands on` (`reference: s 220ג(ג) to paragraph (4) of s 220ד(א)`) (Date 1 8 2025) EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `the target stands on` (`reference: s 220ג(ג) to paragraph (4) of s 220ד(א)`) (Date 10 11 2026) EQUALS JUST FALSE
-- On the printed day itself the words do not settle the question (fork E1 in NOTES.md), and before it this row reads no day on which the paragraph began: NOTHING.
#ASSERT `the target stands on` (`reference: s 220ג(ג) to paragraph (4) of s 220ד(א)`) (Date 31 7 2025) EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `the target stands on` (`reference: s 220ג(ג) to paragraph (4) of s 220ד(א)`) (Date 6 7 2022) EQUALS NOTHING
-- The control subsection prints no day, so the row has no answer for it on any day: NOTHING.
#ASSERT `the target stands on` (`reference: s 220ג(ג) to subsection (ב) of s 220ג`) (Date 10 11 2026) EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `the target stands on` (`reference: s 220ג(ג) to subsection (ב) of s 220ג`) (Date 1 8 2025) EQUALS NOTHING

§ `Tests of the date pairs`

-- Each Hebrew date printed with a Gregorian date gives that Gregorian date in the routine, and the printed pairs are the ones typed.
#ASSERT `the printed pair matches the routine` (`date pair: the printed end of paragraph (4) of s 220ד(א)`)
#ASSERT `the printed pair matches the routine` (`date pair: the issue date in the footer of printed p. 1017`)
#ASSERT (`date pair: the printed end of paragraph (4) of s 220ד(א)`)'s `the Hebrew date, transliterated` EQUALS "6 Av 5785"
#ASSERT (`date pair: the printed end of paragraph (4) of s 220ד(א)`)'s `the Gregorian date printed with it` EQUALS Date 31 7 2025
#ASSERT (`date pair: the issue date in the footer of printed p. 1017`)'s `the Hebrew date, transliterated` EQUALS "7 Tammuz 5782"
#ASSERT (`date pair: the issue date in the footer of printed p. 1017`)'s `the Gregorian date printed with it` EQUALS Date 6 7 2022
-- The last day printed in the paragraph is the Gregorian date of its own printed pair.
#ASSERT (`reference: s 220ג(ג) to paragraph (4) of s 220ד(א)`)'s `the last day printed in the target` EQUALS JUST ((`date pair: the printed end of paragraph (4) of s 220ד(א)`)'s `the Gregorian date printed with it`)

§ `Tests of what was read from where`

-- Both limbs of both citations were read from the official page; that no later instrument touched the words is CONSOLIDATION-ONLY for each.
#ASSERT (`reference: s 220ג(ג) to paragraph (4) of s 220ד(א)`)'s `limb (a) was read from` EQUALS `the official instrument, read from its page image; that no later instrument touched the words is CONSOLIDATION-ONLY`
#ASSERT (`reference: s 220ג(ג) to paragraph (4) of s 220ד(א)`)'s `limb (b) was read from` EQUALS `the official instrument, read from its page image; that no later instrument touched the words is CONSOLIDATION-ONLY`
#ASSERT (`reference: s 220ג(ג) to subsection (ב) of s 220ג`)'s `limb (a) was read from` EQUALS `the official instrument, read from its page image; that no later instrument touched the words is CONSOLIDATION-ONLY`
#ASSERT (`reference: s 220ג(ג) to subsection (ב) of s 220ג`)'s `limb (b) was read from` EQUALS `the official instrument, read from its page image; that no later instrument touched the words is CONSOLIDATION-ONLY`
-- The two printed date pairs carry no such caveat: they are the instrument's own words.
#ASSERT (`date pair: the printed end of paragraph (4) of s 220ד(א)`)'s `the pair was read from` EQUALS `the official instrument, read from its page image`
#ASSERT (`date pair: the issue date in the footer of printed p. 1017`)'s `the pair was read from` EQUALS `the official instrument, read from its page image`
